   1               
   2               /  DDT DRIVER (DR1025)
   3               
   4               / DDT - PDP8-DISC SYSTEM
   5               /COPYRIGHT, 1969    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORP., MAYNARD, MASS.
   6               
   7               / DDT USES CORE FROM LOC THRU LOC+377 (2 PAGES)
   8               /
   9               /   INITIALLY IT ALSO USES 172-177,LOC-1200 THRU LOC+377
  10               /   TO PREPARE THE DRIVER FOR USE.
  11               /
  12               / DDT OVERLAYS CORE FROM 200-4577 AND
  13               / USES CELLS 3,4,5.  THE DRIVER MAY BE ANYWHERE ABOVE
  14               / 5777 AND IS SET BY SELECTING A VALUE FOR "LOC".
  15               
  16               /THIS IS THE METHOD:
  17               /
  18               /1) LOAD DDT  PROPER AS FOLLOWS:
  19               / .LOAD
  20               / :IN-R:
  21               / ^
  22               / *OPT-1
  23               / *ST=7600
  24               / ^^
  25               /  .SAVE DDT:200-4577;0
  26               /
  27               /2) SAVE A BLOCK OF CELLS THE SAME LENGTH AS DDT PROPER AS:
  28               /
  29               /  .SAVE USER:200-4577;0
  30               /
  31               /3) LOAD IN DDT DRIVER AND START AT LOC-200 AS:
  32               /
  33               / .LOAD
  34               / *R:
  35               / ^
  36               / *OPT-2
  37               / ST=<LOC-200>
  38               / ^^
  39               / *IN-S:DDT,S:USER
  40               / ^
  41               / ^
  42               / .
  43               /
  44               /4) SAVE DDT DRIVER AS A SYSTEM PROGRAM:
  45               /
  46               / .SAVE DDT!<LOC>-<LOC+377>;<LOC>
  47               / .
  48               
  49               
  50               / ERRORS ARE SHOWN BY "DDT?"
  51               
  52               / THE FOLLOWING THINGS MAY CAUSE ERRORS:
  53               /       1. USER FILE TOO LARGE
  54               /       2. SYSTEM DEVICE READ ERROR
  55               /       3. NO COMMAND DECODER
  56               
